cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the accompanying paper."
title: "tdcfm: time-domain conditional flow matching for seismic velocity model building"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of a conditional flow matching model that generates
  time-domain interval velocity models from an RMS velocity field, sparse well
  logs, a migrated image and a geological-pattern label, together with the
  synthetic dataset generator and the evaluation code.
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-30"
license: MIT
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/zzh020614-wq/TDCFM-SeismicVelocityModeling"
keywords:
  - flow matching
  - generative model
  - seismic velocity model building
  - geophysics
  - deep learning
